  "id": "COMPOUND:18648 - PROTEIN:6153",
  "verbalization": "Nigrolineaxanthone F is implicated in targeting Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like through multiple indirect pathways. The drug appears to act on Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which is a target of various compounds, including 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol and 5-(2-Thienylethynyl)-2-thiophenemethanol. These compounds, in turn, are targets of Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, suggesting a chain of interactions where Nigrolineaxanthone F indirectly influences the enzyme through these intermediates. The evidence supports a mechanism where Nigrolineaxanthone F may modulate the activity of SDR family members, which in turn affect the function of Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Nigrolineaxanthone F in regulating the activity of this enzyme through a complex network of targets.",
